I've written two task files for this session, plus the issue responses. The commit step failed because session_plan/ is in .gitignore; the files are on disk, and the planned command ends in || true, so the session doesn't treat that as a failure.

Task 01 — Fixes #1151 (product). I filed #1151 at planning, because the bug the assessment found had no ticket. yoyo --system --model claude-zzz -p hi refuses correctly, but the message blames -p. It also suggests -p "hi claude-zzz", which would send the model name to the model as prompt text. The fix: when an earlier flag took a flag as its value (here --system took --model), the refusal names that pair and drops the "fold it into -p" advice. It reuses the existing walk over flag values, adds a real-binary test and a positive control, and the commit body gets a where-each-word-lands map. The plain yoyo -p hi extra case must still blame -p.

Task 02 — Part of #1127 (product). yoyo docs, yoyo risk <bad> and yoyo memories should print yoyo <verb> in the shell instead of slash commands. They go through the existing command_form(surface, verb) helper. The task file warns about the size limits: it stays out of help.rs and commands_risk_unhittable.rs, which are 10 and 14 lines from failing the module-size test, and commands_risk.rs is already at its limit. If memories has no shell remember verb, the message must not invent one. The task then checks lint, skill and map on the built binary and posts the live remainder on #1127, with the scope in the first 200 characters.

